<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Dataset Coverage and Axis-wise Performance</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Prompt taxonomy and distributions</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We annotate all 125 prompts along four orthogonal axes. Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ A.1 Prompt taxonomy and distributions ‣ Appendix A Dataset Coverage and Axis-wise Performance ‣ AcT2I: Evaluating and Improving Action Depiction inText-to-Image Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> defines the axes with category rules and examples; Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ A.1 Prompt taxonomy and distributions ‣ Appendix A Dataset Coverage and Axis-wise Performance ‣ AcT2I: Evaluating and Improving Action Depiction inText-to-Image Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> summarizes coverage and design rationale.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="A1.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Axis</span></span>
</span></th>
